		"name": "Kelaasor Advance Api",
		"description": "## 🧩 Kelaasor API — Overview\n\n### 🎯 Introduction\n\n**Kelaasor API** is a complete backend built with **Django REST Framework**, providing endpoints for user authentication, online course management, purchase workflows, discount systems, support tickets, and an administrative dashboard.\n\nThis Postman collection allows developers and QA engineers to test every workflow — from OTP-based login and course browsing to checkout, order processing, and admin actions — all in one place.\n\n---\n\n### 🔐 Authentication & Authorization\n\nAuthentication is powered by **Simple JWT** combined with an **OTP-based login system**.\n\n- Users authenticate via mobile phone number.\n    \n- Upon OTP verification, the API issues two tokens:\n    - `access` – short-lived bearer token\n        \n    - `refresh` – long-lived token for renewal\n        \n- Tokens are automatically stored in collection variables and applied to all subsequent authorized requests.\n    \n\n**Header format:**\n\n```\nAuthorization: Bearer {{access_token}}\n\n ```\n\n> Public endpoints (such as course catalog) are explicitly marked with `noauth`. \n  \n\n---\n\n### 📂 Folder Structure\n\n#### **1\\. Users (Auth)**\n\nHandles registration, authentication, and password recovery:\n\n- `POST /api/users/register/` — Register a new user\n    \n- `POST /api/users/send-otp/` — Request OTP for login\n    \n- `POST /api/users/verify-otp/` — Verify OTP and obtain JWT tokens\n    \n- `POST /api/users/token/`, `POST /api/users/token/refresh/` — Standard JWT login/refresh\n    \n- `POST /api/users/password/forgot/` and `/password/reset/` — Forgot/reset password flows\n    \n\n#### **2\\. User Panel**\n\nAuthenticated endpoints for end-users:\n\n- `GET /api/user_panel/dashboard/` — Returns user profile, recent orders, tickets, and announcements.\n    \n\n#### **3\\. Courses (Public)**\n\nPublic, read-only course catalog:\n\n- List categories, instructors, and available courses\n    \n- View course detail, chapters, videos, and attachments\n    \n\n#### **4\\. Tickets (User)**\n\nUser-facing support system:\n\n- Create, list, update, and view personal tickets\n    \n- `POST /api/tickets/tickets/reply/` — Add a reply to an existing ticket\n    \n\n#### **5\\. Purchase / Cart / Orders / Discounts**\n\nFull e-commerce workflow:\n\n- `GET /api/purchase/cart/` — Retrieve user cart\n    \n- `POST /api/purchase/cart/add/` — Add a course to cart\n    \n- `GET /api/purchase/orders/` — List all orders\n    \n- `POST /api/purchase/apply-discount/` — Apply a discount code\n    \n- `POST /api/purchase/checkout/` — Finalize checkout and confirm payment\n    \n\n#### **6\\. Admin Panel**\n\nAdministrative APIs for internal staff:\n\n- Manage users, groups, orders, tickets, and discount codes\n    \n- View statistics and notifications\n    \n- Endpoints require staff/admin JWT tokens\n    \n\n---\n\n### ⚙️ Environment Variables\n\n| Variable | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| `base_url` | Base API URL (default: `http://localhost:8000`) |\n| `mobile` | Test user’s mobile number |\n| `otp_code` | Test OTP code (for development) |\n| `access_token` | Access JWT (automatically set after OTP verification) |\n| `refresh_token` | Refresh JWT (automatically set after OTP verification) |\n\n---\n\n### 🧪 Testing Workflow\n\n1. Run **Send OTP** → then **Verify OTP → tokens** to retrieve and store JWTs.\n    \n2. Once tokens are set, all authenticated requests will automatically include them.\n    \n3. For purchasing flow:\n    - Add a course to the cart\n        \n    - Optionally apply a discount code\n        \n    - Call **Checkout** to complete the order\n        \n\n---\n\n### 🧱 Technologies\n\n- **Django REST Framework (DRF)**\n    \n- **Simple JWT** for token-based authentication\n    \n- **PostgreSQL** as the database\n    \n- **Redis / Celery** (optional) for asynchronous OTP delivery\n    \n\n---\n\n### 💡 Developer Notes\n\n- All endpoints are prefixed with `/api/`.\n    \n- Responses are in JSON (UTF-8 encoded).\n    \n- Date/time fields use ISO 8601 format (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`).\n    \n- Standard DRF pagination, filtering, and ordering are supported.\n    \n- Errors follow the DRF pattern with `detail` or `errors` fields.\n    \n\n---\n\n### 📘 Quick Start\n\n1. Import the collection `kelaasor_postman_collection_latest.json`\n    \n2. Import the environment `kelaasor_postman_environment_latest.json`\n    \n3. Set your `base_url` and `mobile` variables\n    \n4. Run the auth flow and begin testing any feature instantly",
